@startuml HermesCLIDocumentAdapters
title Document service: operations, contracts and adapters
top to bottom direction
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
skinparam nodesep 55
skinparam ranksep 60
hide empty members
class "Auth / Users / Workspaces / Documents" as Operations <<application>>
interface "AuthRemote / UsersRemote / WorkspacesRemote / DocumentsRemote" as Port
class "HTTPDocumentClient" as HTTP <<struct>>
class "GRPCDocumentClient" as GRPC <<struct>>
class "FakeDocumentClient" as Fake <<test double>>
class "hermes-document-service" as Server <<external service>>
Operations -down-> Port : calls injected interface
Port <|.. HTTP
Port <|.. GRPC
Port <|.. Fake
HTTP -down-> Server : HTTP API
GRPC -down-> Server : gRPC API
HTTP -[hidden]right-> GRPC
GRPC -[hidden]right-> Fake
note top of Operations
  main creates one selected adapter and injects it here.
  main does not forward runtime requests.
end note
legend bottom
  Dashed triangle = implements; solid arrow = calls.
  Document contracts represent four separate consumer-owned interfaces.
  Production adapters read the token through SessionStore.
  HTTP attaches headers; gRPC attaches metadata.
  Each adapter maps wire DTOs/errors and propagates context/deadlines.
  No universal transport interface; fake requires no network.
  Test application behavior with fakes and adapters with protocol test servers.
  Future live streaming has a separate contract from InboxRemote.
endlegend
@enduml

